  abstract = {The NIH Pragmatic Trials Collaboratory funds trials at **\$500K for planning phase, \$1M/year for implementation**—a tiny fraction of NIH's budget. The ADAPTABLE trial cost **\$14 million** for **15,076 patients** (= **\$929/patient**) versus **\$420 million** for a similar traditional RCT (30x cheaper), yet pragmatic trials remain severely underfunded. PCORnet infrastructure enables real-world trials embedded in healthcare systems, but receives minimal support compared to basic research funding. Additional sources: https://commonfund.nih.gov/hcscollaboratory | https://pcornet.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/ADAPTABLE_Lay_Summary_21JUL2025.pdf | https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5604499/},
